\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The five checks accompanying the transfer-coefficient estimate. The simulated null matters most: at $\kappa = 0$ the \emph  {uncorrected} cross-line cosine is only $0.734$, which read naively reports $27\%$ interaction where the truth is zero, while the disattenuated estimator recovers the truth to within $0.001$. That recovery is what licenses the reference column below. The dose strata carry a molar-resolved dose --- an earlier cache carried the well identifier in the dose field, so what was labelled dose transfer compared physical samples rather than concentrations.}}{43}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:tcontrols}{{10}{43}{The five checks accompanying the transfer-coefficient estimate. The simulated null matters most: at $\kappa = 0$ the \emph {uncorrected} cross-line cosine is only $0.734$, which read naively reports $27\%$ interaction where the truth is zero, while the disattenuated estimator recovers the truth to within $0.001$. That recovery is what licenses the reference column below. The dose strata carry a molar-resolved dose --- an earlier cache carried the well identifier in the dose field, so what was labelled dose transfer compared physical samples rather than concentrations}{table.caption.22}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The transfer coefficient, estimated on real molar doses with dyadic cluster-robust intervals. The matched negative control sits on zero; the same-plate control that produced the earlier false alarm reads $+0.478$ for the reasons given in the text.}}{43}{table.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:transfer}{{11}{43}{The transfer coefficient, estimated on real molar doses with dyadic cluster-robust intervals. The matched negative control sits on zero; the same-plate control that produced the earlier false alarm reads $+0.478$ for the reasons given in the text}{table.caption.23}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces No cell line bends different drugs in a consistent direction. $4{,}000$ pairs per arm; the signal interval at plate scope excludes anything above $+0.002$, so this is a real null rather than an underpowered one. The cell-line-scoped row is wider ($[-0.021, +0.015]$) and carries the claim less strongly.}}{44}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:kappa}{{12}{44}{No cell line bends different drugs in a consistent direction. $4{,}000$ pairs per arm; the signal interval at plate scope excludes anything above $+0.002$, so this is a real null rather than an underpowered one. The cell-line-scoped row is wider ($[-0.021, +0.015]$) and carries the claim less strongly}{table.caption.24}{}}
